<</Title(This study set out to map how downforce, drag and the flow change with ride height for a single front-wing element, find where downforce peaks and why it falls after, and turn that into a ride-height recommendation, using a mesh and solver set-up validated against reference data first)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1830 0 R/Prev 1887 0 R/Next 1858 0 R>>
endobj

1889 0 obj
<</Title(SST treats the whole boundary layer as turbulent, so skin friction is overstated compared to a real wing that stays laminar near the nose. Against the fully turbulent reference, it's +12%. The trends are what the study relies on.)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1858 0 R>>
endobj

