endobj

1933 0 obj
<</Title(The rear wheel carries 5469.9 N at 3 g, but the shock pushes on the frame with 23215 N: 7.6\327 the weight of the whole loaded bike. I first used 17416 N from an assumed 159 mm lever arm; the swingarm study measured 119.28 mm, a 33% higher load.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1913 0 R/Prev 1932 0 R>>
endobj

1934 0 obj
<</Title(The shock pushes the frame up with 23 kN while the swingarm pivot, only 244 mm below, pulls it down. In the original frame that path ran through \33012 solid bars loaded in bending. A \33012 bar only needs the load to act 17 mm off its axis to reach 1692.6 MPa. Even standing still with two riders it sat at 564 MPa, above yield)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1914 0 R>>
endobj

